 	help
-	  Powers up the video codec (VSP) and JPEG codec blocks of the Unisoc UMS9230 and
-	  exposes a register dump in debugfs. It does not decode anything
-	  yet; it is the first step towards a stateless V4L2 decoder.
+	  Powers up the video codec (VSP) and JPEG codec blocks of the Unisoc UMS9230
+	  and exposes a register dump in debugfs. On the VSP it also registers an
+	  EXPERIMENTAL stateless H.264 decoder (intra slices only for now) written
+	  from a reverse-engineered register map; it has not been verified on hardware.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
 	  will be called sprd-vsp.
